finding: "A switch creates its GPU objects and issues every draw in its first frame" is not established, and the removed frame can still contain the selected model's first draw (examples/gltf/tests/scenes.e2e.ts:118-122; also :66-69). The picker label is not a completion barrier: examples/gltf/index.html:42 fires selectScene without awaiting it and :46 immediately mounts the selected label; src/app.ts:59 waits for the model before spawning it. loadGltfScene additionally awaits prepareImages and preparePipelines (src/extras/gltf/scene.ts:367), including async image decode. Therefore a model completing after the first held callback but before the old second callback was presented and exercised by the old test, while the candidate can assert identity/scroll/no-slider on the previous scene and advance without drawing the new selection. The selection counter cancels an unfinished selection when the next choice is made. The two pixel-polled models have a frame-driving retry, but the other models, including compressed ones, have no equivalent barrier. Independent local probe on HEAD: served the example with Vite, exposed the existing world through a response-only HTML-module substitution, and read Viewer.active/models immediately after held frames. No model requests were delayed or replaced. For VertexColorTest, QuantizedMorphCube, OrientationTest, NegativeScaleTest, StainedGlassLamp and AnisotropyBarnLamp the picker had the requested label but Viewer.active after the first frame was still MeshPrimitiveModes. This refutes the unconditional first-frame evidence; it does not claim the old two-frame test guaranteed readiness (in this cold-load probe even its second frame was too early). WebGPU aggregate call counts can count draws of the previous active scene, not prove the requested model rendered. The candidate also no longer executes a second per-selection frame where frame-dependent errors or late pipeline warnings could arise; the global error/warning listeners remain installed but cannot catch work never executed. No concrete existing second-frame-only pipeline/layout defect was reproduced. No model was removed from categories or the loop; the CesiumManCrowd exclusion is unchanged. The pixel polls still drive frames. Hosted timing gates were not rerun by this review.
